// gist — import topology.
//
// The product chassis of the irregex ecosystem: the resident daemon
// transport, the C-ABI plane, the `--generate` primer, and the `gist` face.
// The exact engine beneath is the sibling `irregex` module (reached only
// through `@import("irregex")`; a file import cannot cross a package
// boundary). The `relate` face and its CLI vocabulary moved into the
// `relate` package; they import this chassis for the daemon and the answer
// keep. Judged by `zoning verify`.

package gist {
    // root.zig is the chassis module's public face: it re-exports the cli,
    // session, ffi, and face tiers (what the thin exe main and dependents
    // consume) and aggregates the test step, so it alone may reach anywhere.
    root   src
    facade root.zig
}

// Tiers, low to high. An import may only point back up the page.
zones {
    // The `--generate` primer — man page and shell completions rendered from
    // the face's flag table. Shared face vocabulary (flags, manifest, grade,
    // reprise) moved with the relate face into the `relate` package; what
    // remains is the one generator only this product's man/completions need.
    cli         surface/cli/**

    // The resident session's transport primitives: the wire grammar, the
    // versioned protocol, the daemon image/spawn/vigil lifecycle.
    conduit     exec/session/conduit/**

    // The daemon's self-government: memory rationing and stand-down.
    warden      exec/session/warden/**

    // The daemon proper — dial-or-spawn client and the serve loop over the
    // resident core (which lives in `irregex`, reached as a module). The
    // answer keep's frame types live here too; the relate face reaches them
    // through `@import("gist").session.keep`, not a file import.
    daemon      exec/session/daemon/**

    // C-ABI session + rank producer — the `libgist` surface the Python /
    // Go / Rust bindings link. Kinship/sweep live in relate's ffi; compose
    // lives in blast's. This tier keeps the warm engine, the exact-plane
    // cursors, and `gist_run` for `rank` alone.
    ffi         surface/ffi/**

    // The thin product face. A face imports the chassis; the chassis never
    // imports a face except through root's re-export shelf.
    face        surface/face/**
}

// Reach outside the package: the modules the build graph hands us.
//
// Everything above orders what this package owns. These are the only names it
// says that it does not, and each is a dependency `build.zig` has to satisfy.
// `std`, `builtin` and `root` are the language's, granted without asking.

// The engine, everywhere. This package IS the product chassis over it, so a
// scoped grant would only be a list of every zone: the whole tree compiles
// against `@import("irregex")` because a file import cannot cross a package
// boundary.
use irregex

// The version string, injected by `b.addOptions` — one fact about the build
// that no byte in this tree can know.
use build_options

// A face dispatches through this package's own module rather than by path: a
// binary's root file is its own module root, so relative imports beneath it
// would not resolve, and every driver is analyzed inside the chassis instead.
// It reads as a self-import because it is one; see root.zig's `faces` shelf.
use gist by face

// Guest lists: regions only the named importers may reach at all.

// The face is this package's one product surface. Nothing else in the tree
// reaches into it; a sibling face that wants the same helper takes it from
// below (cli / session), not from beside.
keep surface/face/gist/** to root.zig

// The C-ABI plane is the package's other public face — for callers outside
// Zig. Nothing inside the package consumes its own FFI shims; a Zig caller
// that wants the session takes irregex's `api.zig`, which is what ffi does.
keep surface/ffi/** to root.zig

// Tests are consumers of the architecture, never load-bearing in it.
keep **/*_test.zig to root.zig

// Seals: directories that are deep modules — enter by the entry file.

// The resident session's wire grammar is a cross-language contract — the Zig
// CLI, the Rust binding and the Python binding all speak it — and every frame
// it defines is gated on one negotiated `protocol_version`. Split into the
// opcode spine plus a codec chapter per opcode family (query · result · keep ·
// annals), it is entered as one so a caller binds to the whole versioned
// contract rather than to half of it.
seal exec/session/conduit/protocol through protocol.zig

// Daemon dial + spawn is one decision; a caller that reaches spawn directly
// bypasses the fail-open deadline.
seal exec/session/daemon/client through client.zig

// The resident session's serve loop — split into route/answer/crew/loop,
// entered as one.
seal exec/session/daemon/serve through serve.zig

// Structural laws.
limit  reach to 5 hops
forbid cycles across directories

// Ratified exceptions.
//
// Every one carries the fix that would retire it. An exception that stops
// matching is a hard failure, so paying the debt forces deleting the entry —
// they shrink instead of accreting as folklore.

// The answer-keep CLI passenger (`reprise.zig`) moved into the `relate`
// package with the face that owns it. Its reach into `keep.zig` / `serve.zig`
// is now a module import (`@import("gist").session.*`), so the three
// file-import exceptions that used to live here are gone — the debt was
// retired by the move, not waived.
